        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>An inability to sit still, typically as an aspect of AGITATION or ANXIETY. In people with Parkinson’s disease, akathisia is relatively rare and when it does occur is often an adverse reaction to a medication used to treat the disease.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
