    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Antibiotic -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Antibiotic">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Medicines"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_1289"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <Synonyms>Antibiotic Agents</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Antibiotic Drugs</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Antibiotic Therapy</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Antibiotics</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>antibiotic</Synonyms>
        <definition>Substances naturally produced by microorganisms or their derivatives that selectively target microorganisms not humans. Antibiotics kill or inhibit the growth of microorganisms by targeting components of the microbial cell absent from human cells, including bacterial cell walls, cell membrane, and 30S or 50S ribosomal subunits. These substances are used in the treatment of bacterial and other microbial infections.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C258</definition>
        <reference>NCIT:C258</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Antibiotic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Anticholinergic_drugs -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Anticholinergic_drugs">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Medicines"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/Parkinson_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <Synonyms>Anticholinergic Agent</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Cholinergic Antagonist</Synonyms>
        <definition>Any agent that binds to and blocks nicotinic and/or muscarinic receptors, thereby preventing the actions of the neurotransmitter acetylcholine (Ach) at these receptors.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C66880</definition>
        <reference>NCIT:C66880</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Anticholinergic drugs</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Antidiabetic -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Antidiabetic">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Medicines"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_332"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/Parkinson_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Alzheimer_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Alzheimer_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <Synonyms>Agent, Antidiabetic</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Agent, Antihyperglycemic</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Agent, Hypoglycemic</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Anti-diabetic Agent</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Anti-diabetics</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Antidiabetic Agent</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Antidiabetic Drug</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Hypoglycemic Agents</Synonyms>
        <definition>Any substance used to reduce hyperglycemia or treat disorders associated with diabetes. Based on their mechanism of action, this class of agents can be classified to the following groups: directly acting insulomimetics, which activates insulin receptors; indirectly acting insulinomimetics, which increase insulin release such as sulfonylureas or which potentiate the effect of insulin such as metformin; those act directly on the metabolism of glucose such as inhibitors of glucosidases and inhibitors of aldose reductase.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C29711</definition>
        <reference>NCIT:C29711</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Antidiabetic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


