            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <PMID>PMID:16287153</PMID>
        <Synonyms>consumption of beef</Synonyms>
        <definition>The meat of domestic cattle.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C71932</definition>
        <description>&gt; 1 time/week: OR(95%CI): 1.9(1.1, 3.5)
Reported frequent consumption of beef and beef products thought likely to contain mechanically recovered or head meat, or both, including burgers and meat pies, was associated with increased risk for vCJD</description>
        <reference>NCIT:C71932</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Beef</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Beer -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Beer">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Alcohol"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/Parkinson_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <PMID>PMID:12891669</PMID>
        <PMID>PMID:23840473</PMID>
        <Synonyms>Beer (substance)</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Beer intake</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>beer beverage</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>beer or beer-like beverage</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>hop juice</Synonyms>
        <definition>A carbonated alcoholic beverage made through the fermentation of sugars derived from malted grains; this beverage is usually flavored with hops but other herbs or fruit may be used to enhance its flavor.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C66824</definition>
        <description>Beer, &gt;=4 drinks/month: RR(95%CI): 0.6 (0.5, 0.9)
Beer, 1-3 drinks/month: RR(95%CI): 0.7 (0.5, 0.9)
Compared with those who consumed beer less than once per month, the relative rate (95% confidence interval) was 0.7 (0.5-0.9) for one to three drinks of beer per month, and 0.7 (0.5, 0.9) for one or more drinks of beer per week.</description>
        <description>Beer, Less than 13g/day(1 drink/day): OR(95%CI): 1.00 (0.88, 1.12)
Low to moderate beer consumption with lower PD risk and greater liquor consumption with higher risk. These findings and potential underlying mechanisms warrant further investigations.</description>
        <reference>NCIT:C66824</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Beer</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


