        <Synonyms>Cock</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Hen</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Rooster</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>chicken meat</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>chickens</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>consumption of chicken</Synonyms>
        <definition>A whole chicken. A chicken which is dead or alive and has a relatively intact body.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411457</definition>
        <description>&gt;= 4 servings/week: Mortality(RR(95%CI)): 0.52 (0.32, 0.85)
The strongest finding was an inverse association between chicken consumption and risk of ALS.
[url: https://ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18300717]</description>
        <reference>FOODON:03411457</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Chicken</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Childhood_onset_dystonia -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Childhood_onset_dystonia">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Primary_dystonia"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Jankovic, J. J. T. E., &amp; Tolosa. (2007). Parkinson&apos;s disease and movement disorders. E. Tolosa (Ed.). Lippincott Williams &amp; Wilkins.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>childhood onset symptomatic dystonia</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>childhood-onset dystonia</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>childhood-onset generalized dystonia</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>early onset dystonia</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Early-onset generalized dystonia is characterized by the twisting of the limbs, specifically the foot and leg or hand and arm. The spasms may spread to involve twisting contractions of other parts of the body.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Childhood onset dystonia</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Classical_essential_tremor -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Classical_essential_tremor">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Essential_tremor"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Jankovic, J. J. T. E., &amp; Tolosa. (2007). Parkinson&apos;s disease and movement disorders. E. Tolosa (Ed.). Lippincott Williams &amp; Wilkins.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>classical ET</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>A monosymptomatic, predominant postural and action tremor that is usually slowly progressive over time. </rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Classical essential tremor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


