    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Dairy_products -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Dairy_products">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Food"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#contradictory_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_11949"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#contradictory_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_332"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/Parkinson_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <Synonyms>Dairy Product</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Dairy foods</Synonyms>
        <definition>Raw and processed or manufactured milk and milk-derived products. These are usually from cows (bovine) but are also from goats, sheep, reindeer, and water buffalo.
http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D003611</definition>
        <description>higher dairy intake: OR(95% CI): 1.7(1.12-2.60)
our findings provide further support for a causal relationship between dairy intake and higher PD risk.
[url:https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34997937/]

&gt;502 g/day: RR(95%CI): 1.6 (1.0, 2.5)
These data suggest that dairy consumption may increase the risk of Parkinson&apos;s disease, particularly in men. More studies are needed to further examine these findings and to explore underlying mechanisms.
[url:https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17272289/]

&gt;2.9 servings/day: RR(95%CI): 1.8 (1.2, 2.8)
Our results suggest that higher intake of dairy products may increase the risk of PD in men.
[url:https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12447934/]</description>
        <reference>mesh:D003611</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Dairy products</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


