        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Non-motor_symptom_of_Parkinson_disease"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Mosley A.D., Romaine D.S. &amp; Samii A. (2010) The Encyclopedia of Parkinson&apos;s Disease. Infobase Publishing.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Excessive and even drenching episodes of sweating are common in Parkinson’s, particularly in mid to late stages of the disease, when OFFSTATES begin to occur. Excessive sweating can be a consequence of damage to the autonomic NERVOUS SYSTEM as Parkinson’s progresses or a side effect of ANTI-PARKINSON’S MEDICATIONS.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Excessive sweating</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


