        <Synonyms>Football, American</Synonyms>
        <definition>A competitive team sport played on a rectangular field.This is the American version of the game. It does not include non-North American football (= SOCCER).
http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D005538</definition>
        <reference>mesh:D005538</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Football</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Freezing -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Freezing">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Gait_disturbance"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Jankovic, J. (2008). Parkinson’s disease: clinical features and diagnosis. Journal of Neurology, Neurosurgery &amp; Psychiatry, 79(4), 368-376.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>FOG</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>freezing of gait</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>gait and freezing</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>gait freezing</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>gait-related mobility</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>magnetic feet</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>motor blocks</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Freezing is a form of akinesia and is one of the most disabling symptoms of PD and has five subtypes.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Freezing</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Frontotemporal_Lobar_Degeneration -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Frontotemporal_Lobar_Degeneration">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#TDP-43_Proteinopathies"/>
        <Synonyms>Degeneration, Frontotemporal Lobar</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Degenerations, Frontotemporal Lobar</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>FTLD</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>FTLDs</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Frontotemporal Lobar Degenerations</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Lobar Degeneration, Frontotemporal</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Lobar Degenerations, Frontotemporal</Synonyms>
        <definition>Heterogeneous group of neurodegenerative disorders characterized by frontal and temporal lobe atrophy associated with neuronal loss, gliosis, and dementia. Patients exhibit progressive changes in social, behavioral, and/or language function. Multiple subtypes or forms are recognized based on presence or absence of TAU PROTEIN inclusions. FTLD includes three clinical syndromes: FRONTOTEMPORAL DEMENTIA, semantic dementia, and PRIMARY PROGRESSIVE NONFLUENT APHASIA.
http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D057174</definition>
        <reference>mesh:D057174</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Frontotemporal Lobar Degeneration</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Fruit -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Fruit">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Food"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_332"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Alzheimer_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#OR"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#rational"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <PMID>PMID:23710627</PMID>
        <PMID>PMID:25408208</PMID>
        <Synonyms>FRUIT, UNSPECIFIED</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Fructus/Fruit</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Fruits</Synonyms>
        <definition>A structure consisting of the fertilized and mature ovules (&quot;seeds&quot;) and the ovary wall, which may be fleshy (as in the apple) or dry and hard (as in a maple fruit.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C71972</definition>
        <description>&gt; 21 serving/week: OR(95%CI): 0.265 (0.11, 0.65)
The intake of fruits and beta-carotene decreases the risk of sporadic ALS in this present study.
[url:https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23710627]</description>
        <description>&gt;= 3 pieces/day: Mortality(HR(95%CI)): 0.39(0.22, 0.67)
2-3 pieces/day: Mortality(HR(95%CI)): 0.60(0.39, 0.91)
Exercise, statin, and fruit intake were associated with lower risk for AD mortality.
[url:https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25408208]</description>
        <reference>NCIT:C71972</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Fruit</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Fungus -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Fungus">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Nutrient_substance"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/Parkinson_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Alzheimer_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <Synonyms>FUNGI</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>FUNGUS</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Fungi</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>fungi</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>fungus</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>funguses</Synonyms>
        <definition>A kingdom of eukaryotic, heterotrophic organisms that live as saprobes or parasites, including mushrooms, yeasts, smuts, molds, etc. They reproduce either sexually or asexually, and have life cycles that range from simple to complex. Filamentous fungi refer to those that grow as multicellular colonies (mushrooms and molds).
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C14209</definition>
        <reference>NCIT:C14209</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Fungus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


