            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <Synonyms>general medical history</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>past medical history</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>personal health record</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>personal history</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>personal medical history</Synonyms>
        <definition>In a medical encounter, the physician generally will interview the patient about his or her current problem, and may perform additional testing. The past medical history (PMH) in contrast records information about the patient&apos;s medical, personal and family history that might be relevant to the presenting illness or to provide optimal clinical management. The PMH generally includes (if relevant) other major illnesses, hospitalizations, surgeries, injuries, allergies, gynecologic and obstetric history, family history, personal history including occupational history, alcohol and drug use, etc. 
[url:http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0032443]</definition>
        <reference>HP:0032443</reference>
        <reference>NCIT:C18772</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Medical history</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


