                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Alzheimer_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <PMID>PMID:26170247</PMID>
        <Synonyms>Abelmoschus esculentus</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>ochro</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>okro</Synonyms>
        <definition>Cultivated in tropical, subtropical, and warm temperate regions around the world for its edible green seed pods, okra is used in the cuisines of many countries.
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Okra
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C72033</definition>
        <definition>NCIT:C72033</definition>
        <definition>okra could potentially prevent or halt the initiation of neurodegenerative diseases, particularly in people carrying a H63D polymorphism, or in elderly persons who are at increased risk of AD and ALS.
[url:https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26170247/]</definition>
        <rdfs:label>Okra</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Olfactory_dysfunction -->

