    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Pisa-syndrome -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Pisa-syndrome">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Long_term_complication_of_medication"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Doherty, K. M., Davagnanam, I., Molloy, S., Silveira-Moriyama, L., &amp; Lees, A. J. (2013). Pisa syndrome in Parkinson&apos;s disease: a mobile or fixed deformity?. Journal of Neurology, Neurosurgery &amp; Psychiatry.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>pisa syndrome</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Pisa syndrome is defined as &gt;10° lateral flexion in the standing position,1 and it has been suggested that in the context of Parkinson&apos;s disease (PD) it is an axial dystonia analogous to that seen as a rare consequence of neuroleptic therapy.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Pisa-syndrome</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Plant_Extracts -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Plant_Extracts">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Nutrient_substance"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_332"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/Parkinson_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Alzheimer_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <Synonyms>Substance of plant origin</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>extracts of plant</Synonyms>
        <definition>Plant extracts refer to substances obtained from plants (whole or parts) using appropriate solvents or methods through extraction or processing, which can be applied in pharmaceuticals, food, cosmetics, and other industries.
[ICD-11]  [NIH]  [WHO]</definition>
        <definition>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMIT_0011909</definition>
        <reference>European Food Safety Authority (EFSA). (2022). &quot;Risk Assessment of Plant-Derived Food Additives&quot;.</reference>
        <reference>Journal of Ethnopharmacology. (2020). &quot;Toxicity and Safety Profile of Common Plant Extracts&quot;.</reference>
        <reference>National Institutes of Health (NIH). (2021). &quot;Role of Plant-Derived Compounds in Antioxidant Therapy&quot;. PubMed Central.</reference>
        <reference>OMIT:0011909</reference>
        <reference>World Health Organization (WHO). (2019). &quot;Guidelines for the Safe Use of Plant-Based Cosmetics&quot;.</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Plant Extracts</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Poisoning -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Poisoning">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Epidemiological_factors"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/Parkinson_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <Synonyms>Poisonings</Synonyms>
        <reference>Injury to the body or interference of normal body functions by a substance that is swallowed, inhaled, injected, or absorbed.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C34933</reference>
        <reference>NCIT:C34933</reference>
        <reference>mesh:D011041</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Poisoning</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Pomegranate -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Pomegranate">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Fruit"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Alzheimer_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <PMID>PMID:25441596</PMID>
        <Synonyms>Punica granatum</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>pomegranate food product</Synonyms>
        <definition>A berry fruit of a pomegranate plant (Punica granatum).
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00003679</definition>
        <description>Our results suggest that dietary supplementation with pomegranates may slow the progression of cognitive and behavioral impairments in AD</description>
        <reference>FOODON:00003679</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Pomegranate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Position-specific_postural_tremor -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Position-specific_postural_tremor">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Postural_tremor"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Jankovic, J. J. T. E., &amp; Tolosa. (2007). Parkinson&apos;s disease and movement disorders. E. Tolosa (Ed.). Lippincott Williams &amp; Wilkins.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>A rare variant of postural tremor.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Position-specific postural tremor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Position_specific_tremor -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Position_specific_tremor">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Primary_writing_tremor"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Jankovic, J. J. T. E., &amp; Tolosa. (2007). Parkinson&apos;s disease and movement disorders. E. Tolosa (Ed.). Lippincott Williams &amp; Wilkins.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>type B tremor</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Position-specific tremor occurs when the hand position used in writing is adopted.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Position specific tremor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Postural_instability -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Postural_instability">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Motor_symptom_of_Parkinson_disease"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Jankovic, J. (2008). Parkinson’s disease: clinical features and diagnosis. Journal of Neurology, Neurosurgery &amp; Psychiatry, 79(4), 368-376.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>PI</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Postural instability due to loss of postural reflexes is generally a manifestation of the late stages of PD and usually occurs after the onset of other clinical features.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Postural instability</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Postural_tremor -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Postural_tremor">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Parkinsonian_tremor"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Jankovic, J. J. T. E., &amp; Tolosa. (2007). Parkinson&apos;s disease and movement disorders. E. Tolosa (Ed.). Lippincott Williams &amp; Wilkins.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Postural tremor is present while voluntarily maintaining a position against gravity.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Postural tremor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Potato -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Potato">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Vegetable"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/Parkinson_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <PMID>PMID:29136149</PMID>
        <Synonyms>potatoes</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>spud</Synonyms>
        <definition>The edible tuber of Solanum tuberosum.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C72045</definition>
        <description>risk of PD is increased in farmers exposed to pesticides on several French crops and livestock.</description>
        <reference>NCIT:C72045</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Potato</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Primary_dystonia -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Primary_dystonia">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Continual_dystonia"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Jankovic, J. J. T. E., &amp; Tolosa. (2007). Parkinson&apos;s disease and movement disorders. E. Tolosa (Ed.). Lippincott Williams &amp; Wilkins.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>It describes a case in which the dystonia is the only neurological disorder that the person has. Primary dystonias include some genetic forms (such as DYT1 dystonia in which a gene has been identified) and forms for which a cause is not usually found. </rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Primary dystonia</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Primary_orthostatic_tremor -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Primary_orthostatic_tremor">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Other_essential_tremor"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Jankovic, J. J. T. E., &amp; Tolosa. (2007). Parkinson&apos;s disease and movement disorders. E. Tolosa (Ed.). Lippincott Williams &amp; Wilkins.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>A unique tremor syndrome that has been observed until now only in patients over 40 years old and is characterized by a subjective feeling of unsteadiness during stance but only in severe cases during gait.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Primary orthostatic tremor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Primary_writing_tremor -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Primary_writing_tremor">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Other_essential_tremor"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Jankovic, J. J. T. E., &amp; Tolosa. (2007). Parkinson&apos;s disease and movement disorders. E. Tolosa (Ed.). Lippincott Williams &amp; Wilkins.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Tremor during writing without other manifestations of tremor or other neurological disease is called primary writing tremor.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Primary writing tremor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Processed_foods_and_other_foods -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Processed_foods_and_other_foods">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Food"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#contradictory_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_332"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_11949"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <Synonyms>processed food</Synonyms>
        <definition>A processed food is the result of the process of home or industrial food preparation.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ONS_0000100</definition>
        <reference>ONS:0000100</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Processed foods and other foods</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Processed_meat -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Processed_meat">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Meat"/>
        <Synonyms>processed meat food product</Synonyms>
        <definition>A processed food product consisting of meat which has been subjected to preservation and/or taste altering processes such as grinding, salting, curing, fermentation, smoking, and addition of chemical preservatives.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001010</definition>
        <reference>FOODON:00001010</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Processed meat</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Progressive_Supranuclear_Palsy -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Progressive_Supranuclear_Palsy">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_680"/>
        <Synonyms>Progressive supranuclear ophthalmoplegia</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Steele-Richardson-Olszewski Syndrome</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>Supranuclear Palsy, Progressive</Synonyms>
        <definition>A rare neurodegenerative disorder characterized by gait and balance difficulties and loss of coordination of eye movements.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C85028</definition>
        <reference>NCIT:C85028</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Progressive Supranuclear Palsy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Proprietary_concentrate_feed_used -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Proprietary_concentrate_feed_used">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Animal_feed"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Bovine_Spongiform_Encephalopathy"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <PMID>PMID:16617042</PMID>
        <definition>Less than 12 months of age: OR(95%CI): 15.6(7.3, 34.9)
The results indicated that in comparison with these control farms a higher proportion of the BSE farms had also kept pigs or poultry, although the difference was not significant, and that a significantly higher proportion of the BSE farms had fed proprietary concentrates and/or milk replacers to their calves.</definition>
        <rdfs:label>Proprietary concentrate feed used</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Pseudobulbar_affect -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Pseudobulbar_affect">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Non-motor_symptom_of_Amyotrophic_lateral_sclerosis"/>
        <rdfs:label>Pseudobulbar affect</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Psychology -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Psychology">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Lifestyle_factor"/>
        <Synonyms>NCIT:C189161</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>[Behavioral or Psychological Factor]
A factor that is associated with an individual&apos;s thoughts or conduct.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C189161</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>psychological factor</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>psychology</Synonyms>
        <definition>The study of behavior and cognition.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C17027</definition>
        <reference>NCIT:C17027</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Psychology</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Psychosis -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Psychosis">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Neuropsychiatric_dysfunction"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Mosley A.D., Romaine D.S. &amp; Samii A. (2010) The Encyclopedia of Parkinson&apos;s Disease. Infobase Publishing.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>A condition of mental dysfunction in which a person loses contact with reality. DELUSIONS, HALLUCINATIONS, CONFUSION, DISORIENTATION, and PARANOIA are common in psychosis. In the person with Parkinson’s disease, psychosis can develop as a separate disease entity, as a manifestation of the brain deterioration taking place as a result of the Parkinson’s, or as a side effect of ANTIPARKINSON’S MEDICATIONS.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Psychosis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Pulsion -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Pulsion">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Gait_disturbance"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Mosley, A. D., Romaine, D. S., &amp; Samii, A. (2010). The Encyclopedia of Parkinson&apos;s Disease. Infobase Publishing.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>antepulsion</Ontology1296772722296:synonyms>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>pulsion is the tendency to step forward when bumped or bumping into an object.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Pulsion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Punding -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Punding">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Non-motor_symptom_of_Parkinson_disease"/>
        <Ontology1296772722296:Reference>Evans, A. H., Katzenschlager, R., Paviour, D., O&apos;Sullivan, J. D., Appel, S., Lawrence, A. D., &amp; Lees, A. J. (2004). Punding in Parkinson&apos;s disease: its relation to the dopamine dysregulation syndrome. Movement disorders, 19(4), 397-405.</Ontology1296772722296:Reference>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Punding is a term that was coined originally to describe complex prolonged, purposeless, and stereotyped behaviour in chronic amphetamine users.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>Punding</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Purchase_of_feedstuffs_for_poultry -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Purchase_of_feedstuffs_for_poultry">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Animal_feed"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Bovine_Spongiform_Encephalopathy"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <PMID>PMID:17425937</PMID>
        <definition>OR(95%CI): 1.8(1.1, 3)
To a lesser extent, on-farm cross-contaminations, i.e. consumption by cattle of feedstuffs initially dedicated to other animals and which could legally contain MBM, have probably also existed, since the presence on farms of poultry fed purchased feed involved an increased risk of BSE.</definition>
        <rdfs:label>Purchase of feedstuffs for poultry</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#QPCTL -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#QPCTL">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#protein-coding_gene"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
