        <reference>www.medicalnewstoday.com</reference>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy> Symptom is something the patient feels and describes. Parkinson’s disease causes problems with movement, cognitive problems, neurobehavioral problems, as well as sensory and sleep difficulties. The signs and symptoms usually begin gradually, slowly and often randomly (in no set order).
</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
