    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Whale_meat -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Whale_meat">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Fish"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/Parkinson_disease"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <PMID>PMID:18455239</PMID>
        <Synonyms>mesh:D014907</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>whale meat food product</Synonyms>
        <definition>Large marine mammals of the order CETACEA. In the past, they were commercially valued for whale oil, for their flesh as human food and in ANIMAL FEED and FERTILIZERS, and for baleen. Today, there is a moratorium on most commercial whaling, as all species are either listed as endangered or threatened.
http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D014907</definition>
        <description>Often whale meat consumption: OR(95%CI): 6.53 (3.02, 14.14)
Increased intake of whale meat and blubber in adult life was significantly associated with PD, thus suggesting a positive association between previous exposure to marine food contaminants and development of PD.</description>
        <reference>FOODON:00002346</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Whale meat</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#White_meat -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#White_meat">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Meat"/>
        <Synonyms>consumption of white meat</Synonyms>
        <definition>In culinary terms, white meat is meat which is pale in color before and after cooking. In traditional gastronomy, white meat also includes rabbit, the flesh of milk-fed young mammals (in particular veal and lamb), and sometimes pork. In ecotrophology and nutritional studies, white meat includes poultry and fish, but excludes all mammal flesh, which is considered red meat.
[wikipedia]</definition>
        <reference>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_meat</reference>
        <rdfs:label>White meat</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Wild_mushroom -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Wild_mushroom">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Vegetable"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#harmful_effect"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_332"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <PMID>PMID:34216974</PMID>
        <Synonyms>Wild mushrooms</Synonyms>
        <Synonyms>toadstool</Synonyms>
        <definition>A mushroom or toadstool is the fleshy, spore-bearing fruiting body of a fungus, typically produced above ground on soil or another food source. 
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mushroom
Includes any product that can be described/observed as several types of fresh mushrooms sparsely cultivated or found wild which should be identified on attribute level. Specifically excludes: Prepared, Processed and Shelf Stable wild mushrooms, excludes LanguaL curation note: Index geographical origin in facet R, growing method (conventional, organic) in facet Z, and variety in facet B.
http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03401559</definition>
        <description>This finding supports the hypothesis that genotoxins of fungal origin may induce motor neuron degeneration.</description>
        <reference>FOODON:03401559</reference>
        <rdfs:label>Wild mushroom</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Wine -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Wine">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#Alcohol"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/NDDRFO#beneficial_effect"/>
